        "The cash book is both journal and ledger: its debit side records receipts, its credit side payments, and bank columns reconcile directly with statements. Analysed cash books with columns for rent, wages and sundries collapse many postings into one. Petty cash runs on the imprest system: a float of, say, N20,000 is restored at intervals by the exact amount of vouchers spent. Cash and credit trading are recorded separately in {S} so control accounts can police the personal ledgers.",
