        "Errors that do not break the trial balance include error of principle, such as debiting motor expenses instead of motor vehicles; error of complete omission; error of commission, posting to the wrong customer's account; compensating errors; and original entry errors. A casting error or a one-sided posting breaks it. Each error class has a standard correction entry in {S}, and examination questions expect the debit and credit named precisely, not a vague restatement.",
