        "Direction errors in reconciliation are the commonest: students add the stock adjustment when they should subtract, or apply the fixed overhead rate of the wrong year. Anchor on the rule, absorption profit is higher when stock rises, and test your direction against it. That one sentence resolves most reconciliation traps set in {S} papers.",
