        ("mcq", "A flexible budget with fixed N3,600,000 and variable N900 per unit at 10,000 units totals",
         "N12,600,000", ["N14,400,000", "N9,000,000", "N12,000,000"],
         "Fixed stands at 3,600,000 while variable flexes to 9,000,000."),
        ("mcq", "In {S}, zero-based budgeting requires",
         "justifying every activity afresh through ranked decision packages",
         ["adding a percentage to last year's figures", "copying last year unchanged", "flexing costs for actual output"],
         "Each naira must be justified from zero, unlike incremental budgeting."),
        ("mcq", "Standard price N800, actual price N780 on actual usage of 8,200 kg. The price variance is",
         "N164,000 favourable", ["N164,000 adverse", "N160,000 favourable", "N80,000 favourable"],
         "Two naira saved per kilogram on 8,200 kg gives N164,000."),
        ("mcq", "Standard usage 8,100 kg against actual 8,200 kg at a standard price of N800. The usage variance is",
         "N80,000 adverse", ["N80,000 favourable", "N100,000 adverse", "N84,000 adverse"],
         "The extra 100 kg at standard price costs N80,000."),
        ("mcq", "Standard material cost N6,480,000 against actual N6,396,000. The total material cost variance is",
         "N84,000 favourable", ["N84,000 adverse", "N244,000 favourable", "N16,000 adverse"],
         "Actual below standard is favourable, and 164,000 minus 80,000 confirms N84,000."),
        ("mcq", "Actual 4,300 hours at N1,250 against a standard rate of N1,200. The rate variance is",
         "N215,000 adverse", ["N215,000 favourable", "N200,000 adverse", "N120,000 adverse"],
         "Fifty naira extra per hour on 4,300 hours gives N215,000."),
        ("mcq", "Standard time is 5 hours per unit; output 840 units. Standard hours allowed are",
         "4,200 hours", ["4,300 hours", "4,000 hours", "4,250 hours"],
         "840 units by 5 hours gives 4,200 standard hours."),
        ("mcq", "Actual 4,300 hours against 4,200 standard hours at N1,200. The efficiency variance is",
         "N120,000 adverse", ["N120,000 favourable", "N100,000 adverse", "N125,000 adverse"],
         "The 100 excess hours at standard rate cost N120,000."),
        ("mcq", "In {S}, an adverse variance means",
         "actual profit is lower than the standard allowed", ["actual profit is higher", "cash has run out", "the standard was wrong"],
         "Adverse describes the profit effect, whatever the operational cause."),
        ("mcq", "A sales budget of 2,000 units at N5,000 each totals",
         "N10,000,000", ["N1,000,000", "N10,500,000", "N2,000,000"],
         "Volume times price is the revenue line of the sales budget."),
        ("mcq", "In {S}, management by exception directs attention to",
         "significant deviations from plan", ["all results equally", "only favourable variances", "fixed costs only"],
         "Thresholds and repetition decide which variances deserve investigation."),
        ("mcq", "A favourable price variance with an adverse usage variance may indicate",
         "cheaper material of lower quality", ["better purchasing with no side effects", "an arithmetic error", "higher selling prices"],
         "Interdependent variances must be read together before judging the buyer."),
        ("mcq", "Under absorption costing, the fixed overhead volume variance measures",
         "under- or over-absorption caused by activity differences", ["spending differences", "sales mix changes", "cash flow gaps"],
         "Volume variance isolates the effect of working above or below budgeted activity."),
        ("mcq", "The production budget is derived from",
         "the sales budget adjusted for the stock policy", ["the cash budget", "the purchases budget", "the capital budget"],
         "Required production equals budgeted sales plus desired closing stock minus opening stock."),
        ("mcq", "In {S}, a budget committee exists to",
         "coordinate and approve the functional budgets", ["prepare tax returns", "set labour standards only", "audit the accounts"],
         "Coordination keeps the interlocking budgets consistent before the master budget assembles."),
        ("tf", "The master budget summarises all functional budgets into forecast financial statements.",
         "True", ["False"],
         "It assembles the budgeted income statement, balance sheet and cash budget."),
